He pushed his sunglasses back into place with his middle finger. “You
made the right call. What are your plans?”
“I don’t have any.”
“Where are you?”
She blinked. “In Lisbon.”
“I know that, bebe. Where in Lisbon?”
“Uh…” She turned the camera around, so he could see the stores lining
the street.
He snapped his fingers. “I know where you are. I’ll be there in ten.”
“Ten?” she echoed, but the screen had already gone blank. She looked
up and found she was the focus of two disgruntled, disapproving males.
“What?”
