“He’s a nightmare to shadow.”
Wasn’t that the truth. Johnny was just as chaotic, endearing, and
hilarious as she remembered. He was a rambling monologue of information
and observations and had been completely oblivious to Mo and Johan
trailing them from place to place. Johnny’s impulsive, split-second
decisions to hop on trams, slip in and out of stores, or grab a bite to eat kept
Mo and Johan on their toes all day. Johnny managed to lose them without
even trying. Watching her guards struggle to keep up with Johnny kept her
entertained.
She slumped against the wall as they rode the elevator up to her suite. A
day with Johnny is exactly what she needed. He didn’t ask about her life or
